---
title: Laab moo
servings: 2
tags: [pork, gluten-free, quick]
cuisine: thai
time: 30 minutes
source: Authentic Thai Laab with Pork (Laab Moo) by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/laab-moo
---

== Toasted rice powder ==

Put the @jasmine rice{2%tbsp} and @?makrut lime leaf{1} in a dry #pot{} over medium-high heat. Stir constantly until the rice is deep brown. Lift out the leaf as soon as it is crisp. Tip the rice out at once so it does not scorch, and let it cool a little.

Grind the rice and leaf in a #mortar and pestle{} or spice grinder to a sandy powder. Discard any tough stem left behind.

> The powder keeps a month in a sealed jar in the fridge.

== Laab ==

Mash about a third of the @fish sauce{2%tbsp} into the @ground pork{9%oz} with a fork to break it up.

Bring @water{2%tbsp} to a boil in the same pot over high heat. Add the pork and stir, breaking it up, until just cooked through. Take it off the heat straight away.

While it is hot, stir in the @shallot{1/4%cup}(thinly sliced) and @?makrut lime leaves{2}(finely shredded) so the shallot wilts.

Add the rest of the fish sauce, @chili flakes{1-2%tsp}, @?MSG{1/8-1/4%tsp}, the toasted rice powder and @lime juice{2%tbsp}. Taste and adjust.

Let it cool for a minute or two if it is still very hot, then fold in @cilantro{8-10%sprigs}(roughly chopped), @green onion{1}(chopped), @mint leaves{1/4%cup}(large leaves torn) and @?sawtooth coriander{2-3%leaves}(thinly sliced).

Serve warm or at room temperature with sticky rice and raw vegetables: @cabbage{}(green), @cucumber{}, @long beans{}, @romaine lettuce{} or @radishes{}.
